<section class="section section--sand">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Checklists</p>
      <h2>Before and after your procedure</h2>
      <p>General advice. Always follow the personal instructions Dr. Junaid gives you, which take priority.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="info-cols">
      <div class="info-box reveal">
        <h3><i class="fas fa-clipboard-list" aria-hidden="true"></i> Before surgery</h3>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Tell Dr. Junaid about every medicine, supplement and allergy</li>
          <li>Stop smoking and vaping as early as possible; nicotine slows healing</li>
          <li>Ask before taking aspirin, blood thinners or herbal supplements</li>
          <li>Follow fasting instructions if you are having sedation or general anaesthesia</li>
          <li>Arrange someone to take you home and stay with you the first night</li>
          <li>Prepare loose, comfortable clothes and a clean, restful space at home</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="info-box reveal">
        <h3><i class="fas fa-bed" aria-hidden="true"></i> After surgery</h3>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Take medicines exactly as prescribed</li>
          <li>Wear compression garments or dressings as instructed</li>
          <li>Walk gently around the house to keep your circulation moving</li>
          <li>Keep wounds clean and dry, and do not remove stitches yourself</li>
          <li>Avoid heavy lifting, the gym and swimming until you are cleared</li>
          <li>Protect healing skin and scars from strong sun</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <div><strong>Get help straight away</strong> if you have a high fever, bleeding that will not stop, rapidly increasing pain or swelling, chest pain, breathlessness, or a painful swollen calf. Contact the team immediately and, if you feel very unwell, go to the nearest emergency department.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

